  "id": "deskilling",
  "term": "deskilling",
  "definition": "Deskilling is a loss or weakening of professional skills when repeated reliance on automation shifts important thinking and decision-making away from the practitioner. In psychology, it can mean reduced clinical judgment, diagnostic reasoning, or ethical autonomy as these abilities are used less often.",
